TI  - Morphological study of spleen following its torsion in dogs
AU  - Bhadwal, M.S.
AU  - Jalaluddin, A.M.
PY  - 1999
T2  - Indian Veterinary Journal
VL  - 76
IS  - 12
SP  - 1079
EP  - 1081
AB  - Splenic torsion is a complex medical and surgical emergency seen in deep chested large breeds of dogs (Lipowitz, 1977 and George et al., 1984). Grossly enlarged spleen following exploratory laporatory (Howenstein et al., 1975 and Wright and Callahan, 1987) and radiographic splenomegaly (Stevenson et al., 1981) have been reported to be a common finding clinical cases of splenic torsion. However, systematic investigation on morphological alterations in spleen following its torsion is lacking. Hence, this study was planned to generate information on this aspect in dogs.
